Loom: wave32 xor-16 subgroup shuffles lower to v_permlanex16_b32.

kernel.subgroup.shuffle<xor> with offset 16 and width 32 went through ds_swizzle (the DPP xor table stops at 8),
a round trip through the LDS pipe whose lgkmcnt wait also catches every outstanding LDS access. The gfx11 sets get a
v_permlanex16_b32 descriptor with SGPR selectors, and the shuffle lowering uses it with identity selectors
(0x76543210, 0xfedcba98): lane i reads lane i of the other 16-lane row, one VALU op.

Dependent-chain latency per exchange + add (gfx1151 microbench): permlanex16 23.8 vs ds_swizzle 49.8 clock ticks.
Attention softmax exchanges: main twin -1.1..-3% standalone at 2K..8K, 32K prefill chunks 1-7 -1.5..-1.9%; KT2 and
pp2048 flat; decode GEMVs flat. pp2048, 32K and decode outputs bit-identical.
